## Critical Risk Summary for Primary Objective Use

```
double PMeanError(p=2) → vanishing gradients late in training
no axiom weighting    → grounded vs rule axioms compete blindly  
Equiv connective      → bidirectional constraints cause conflicts
safe_forall(0.5)      → silent noise injection into sat aggregation
build_axiom bug       → rule2 is logically wrong, corrupting the objective
```

The `build_axiom` bug I flagged earlier is especially severe here — if `rule2` is silently wrong, your **primary loss is computing the wrong thing from epoch 1**, and your model will converge to a logically incorrect solution with no error signal to tell you.

